# Canvas/WebGL pixel-noise patch — DRAFT v2
#
# Adds per-render micro-noise to 2D canvas readback AND toDataURL AND
# WebGL readPixels, so fingerprinting sites that hash the pixel buffer
# cannot get a stable hash even within a session.
#
# This version completes the toDataURL path that was stubbed in v1:
# the raw bitmap is noised in-place before being passed to the JPEG/PNG
# encoder, so the resulting data URL hash changes while the visible
# pixels stay perceptually identical.
#
# Status: UNVERIFIED — written without Firefox source access. Line
# numbers are approximate. Apply with --fuzz=5, fix .rej manually,
# regenerate:
#
#     cd camoufox-142.0.1-fork.27
#     patch -p1 -i ../patches/canvas-webgl-pixel-noise.patch --fuzz=5
#     git diff > ../patches/canvas-webgl-pixel-noise.patch
#
# MaskConfig keys:
#   canvas:pixel_noise:enabled        bool   default false
#   canvas:pixel_noise:amplitude      int    1..10 (default 2)
#   canvas:pixel_noise:frequency      double 0.0..1.0 (default 0.05)
#   canvas:pixel_noise:seed           int    deterministic per profile
#   webgl:readback_noise:enabled      bool   default false
#   webgl:readback_noise:amplitude    int    1..10 (default 2)
#   webgl:readback_noise:seed         int    deterministic per profile

